ovie's pointlessness  writing it goes on for about an hour and  45 minutes and right up until the second  it ends you keep feeling as if it's just  about to start other critics turn their  ayah towards sony calling morbius an  obvious example of a cynical  money-making machine  charlotte o'sullivan of london evening  standard called it a cash grab so sloppy  it makes you wonder if the top brass of  sony are nihilistic members of the  undead meanwhile others chose to slouch  into the vampire buns like brian lloyd  of entertainment ie who wrote  morbius really does  suck yes we couldn't even come up with  something more inventive folks  to be fair neither could we how far are  we allowed to go  to fix something that's broken  it's not just the movie's general  quality that's drawing the reviewers  ayah several critics have also pointed  out that jared leto who as an academy  award winner clearly has a history of  knowing how to act doesn't quite manage  to impress as a titular character for  various reasons  according to megan navarro of bloody  disgusting letto simply fails to  captivate in the same way as tom hardy  does in his symbiote-filled corner of  sony's universe of marvel characters she  wrote without say someone like tom hardy  embracing the weirdness of the character  in venom it's tough to find rooting  interest or muster any excitement with  the vampiric batman meanwhile stephanie  zakharik of time felt that while leto  does bring an element of emotion in the  movie he perhaps isn't so much a serious  actor as one who takes himself very  seriously  nobody has ever said that to me nobody  michael phillips of the chicago tribune  stepped back to look at the bigger  picture and found that when you combine  mobius with leto's recent turn as paulo  gucci and house of gucci it can be very  difficult to comprehend the actor's ways  the critic wrote i don't relish pinning  blame or a tail or horns or anything on  a particular star but my bafflement  regarding le